WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.060
- [Interviewer] All right, JD,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.930
JD where you grow up,

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.070
where are you from originally?

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.170
- [JD] Originally from
Rural Mountain, Tennessee.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:12.720
- [Interviewer] And did you
have the Klan growing up

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.060
in your family as a kid?

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:17.373
- [J.D.] Yeah, somewhat
on my grandparents side.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.983
- [Interviewer] How did you get involved?

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.330
- Well, around 2015 or so,

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.610
when Dylan Roof, he's took
and shot the black people

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.490
in Charleston in that church,

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:36.490
and every picture that I saw on TV of him,

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:39.150
he was having the
confederate flag in his hand

00:00:40.593 --> 00:00:43.193
and he never was a member
of any organization.

00:00:45.146 --> 00:00:47.750
And then they go and take the flag down

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.580
in South Carolina off the
state capital building

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.260
because of that and I thought maybe,

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.351
that was kind of a slap in the face

00:00:56.351 --> 00:01:00.723
to the south, to our ancestors
that fought in the Civil War.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.300
I had people on both sides
of my family that fought

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.163
in the Civil War for
Tennessee and North Carolina,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.100
and in 2017 I joined
the Loyal White Knights,

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.913
and I just wanted to
get out and try to make,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.883
do my part and try to make a difference.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.000
Like I.W. was saying, if
we don't pull together

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.740
it's gonna be a like a sinking ship,

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.170
our rights are going
down the drain every day

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.590
and I just wish my grandparents was around

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.270
to see me and know that I'm doing my share

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.903
and trying to preserve our history.

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:49.500
And I don't consider
myself really as a racist,

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.480
I'm more of a separatist,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.150
I believe in keeping the races separate.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:57.850
That's what God intended,
that's why he put us

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.683
on different bodies of
land, different language.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.653
Just different cultures all together.

00:02:06.743 --> 00:02:09.150
And I believe that the white race

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.803
is a superior race, and that's just,

00:02:15.417 --> 00:02:17.263
that's kind of the way
I feel about it, so.

00:02:18.113 --> 00:02:19.115
- [Interviewer] What do you

00:02:19.115 --> 00:02:20.591
wish the United States looked like?

00:02:20.591 --> 00:02:22.090
- Sorry?
- What do you

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.150
wish the United States
looked like racially,

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.320
I mean right know we're all very mixed.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:26.600
- Yeah, we're very mixed,

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:31.053
I just wish that they could
stay more to their self.

00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:34.080
- When you say they?
- Don't try to push

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.251
'em down my throat, you know?

00:02:36.251 --> 00:02:37.084
- [Interviewer] When you
say they, you mean--?

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.995
- Our government, and not our government,

00:02:39.995 --> 00:02:44.210
but the black race, the
Hispanics, the Orientals,

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:47.283
I wish that they would
stay with themselves.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.370
And I think the country
would be a lot better off

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:56.370
if it was like that, and
Lincoln, he freed the slaves,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.170
he was from Illinois, so
I think they should've

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.840
gave that state to the slaves

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.780
and let 'em all go to Illinois

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:06.150
if that what he preferred.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.800
I think right now it's a slippery slope

00:03:12.298 --> 00:03:15.460
and if the white people
don't get out there

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.622
and try to make a difference,

00:03:17.622 --> 00:03:20.990
we're gonna give our
history, our heritage away,

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:22.033
I mean, it's gone.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:29.204
But you know, I just wish that more people

00:03:29.204 --> 00:03:33.413
would see the light and see
where this country's heading,

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:36.950
because I give it another 10 years,

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.340
we'll not be able to do
what we're doing today.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:42.170
It's probably gonna be a felony

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.260
to be seen in the Klan hood, so,

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.213
I mean it's just a matter of time.

00:03:48.331 --> 00:03:49.910
- [Interviewer] What is the
Klan's biggest issues today?

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.350
Is it immigration?

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.060
- Well, we're strongly against--

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:58.733
- Race mixing.
- you know, mixing races,

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:03.460
messing with our monuments,
our flag, our history,

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.860
especially in the South,
because we were originated

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:09.030
in the South in Palaska, Tennessee

00:04:10.891 --> 00:04:13.897
and being from Tennessee, you know,

00:04:13.897 --> 00:04:15.990
the Klan's always been
strong in that state,

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:20.990
and in North Carolina, and I just wish

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.790
that we had a better opportunity

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.850
to get out there and make a difference,

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:34.850
because they, they're not
wanting to issue us permits

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.270
and stuff like that to
have rallies or anything,

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:40.390
or public demonstrations,

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.210
but you've got all this
protesting stuff going on,

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.880
and they're just out here
doing what they wanna do

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.280
and tearing up the country,

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.840
and nothing's said, I
mean it's not the Klan,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.770
there's a lot of these other groups,

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.523
they're not doing that.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.600
- [Interviewer] Are
you a religious person?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.881
- Yes sir.

00:05:01.881 --> 00:05:02.714
- [Interviewer] The Klan's
a religious organization.

00:05:02.714 --> 00:05:03.547
- Yes sir.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.730
- [Interviewer] What
aspects of Christianity

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.770
is the basis for the Klan?

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.700
- Well, I'm Souther Baptist.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.675
I'm basically Baptist, I mean,

00:05:12.675 --> 00:05:16.036
there's Methodists,
Presbyterians, you know,

00:05:16.036 --> 00:05:18.963
no Catholics, I mean, it's.

00:05:22.983 --> 00:05:23.930
- [Interviewer] And you
are a Imperial Wizard,

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.390
or a--?
- No, I'm a Grand Dragon,

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:28.040
I'm over North Carolina
and South Carolina.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.727
- [Interviewer] What do you do, okay?

00:05:29.727 --> 00:05:31.020
And what is a grand dragon?

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.693
- It's the state officer,
I'm over the state,

00:05:35.283 --> 00:05:38.433
and I'm right under the
Imperial Wizard, you know.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.500
- [Interviewer] So what is
it about African Americans,

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.373
that you want them to be separate?

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.900
- Well, I don't think God intended

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.550
for them to be mingling with us

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.100
and especially to be breeding

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.393
with the white race.

00:05:55.284 --> 00:05:59.723
It brings about a mongrol
race, I mean a mulatto color.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.540
Nothing makes me any sicker than

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.908
to see a little kid running around

00:06:04.908 --> 00:06:06.545
and their skin's just yellow.

00:06:06.545 --> 00:06:07.695
I mean a mulatto color.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.350
I mean, I wouldn't feel
so bad about the blacks

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.650
if the government wasn't
pushing them down our throat.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.930
Just like in the 60s, I mean,

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.570
they pushed them down our throat

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:23.540
and the schools and cafes, restaurants,

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:28.540
and it's just something that I don't think

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:30.640
should've ever happened.

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.170
- [Interviewer] How has the Klan changed?

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.920
I mean you've only been
a member for a few years.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:39.310
- I've been, yeah several years,

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.860
but the Klan's really changed a lot,

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:46.420
we're not as violent as we used to be,

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.610
back in the 60s they was
some violent Klan groups,

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.113
especially in Mississippi.

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.283
And it gave the Klan a bad rep,

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.307
but today we're more laid back.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:05.360
And it's not a more of a terrorist group

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.920
than what they used to be, they claim

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:10.830
that we're in between
in Nazis and Al Qaeda.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.570
We're ranked number two in the world

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.250
as one of the worst terrorist groups.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.660
I don't see how they
could rank us up there

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.080
like Al Qaeda, or the Nazis.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.723
I mean we don't go out
and just kill people.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.600
- [Interviewer] Have you
traveled to other countries?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:31.680
- No, I've never been in another country,

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.900
but I've been all around
the southern states.

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:36.843
I've not lost nothing up
north, I'm not going up there.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.350
- [Interviewer] So what do
you think about the state

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.030
of our country, and its future.

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:43.943
- Right now, I think it's,

00:07:44.893 --> 00:07:47.140
it's gonna eventually end up in turmoil

00:07:49.103 --> 00:07:53.080
and Donald Trump, he talked
a good talk at first,

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.833
that got him into, that
got him into office.

00:07:57.184 --> 00:07:59.360
- [Interviewer] You'd be voting for Trump?

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.890
- Yeah, I'll vote for
Trump, I did the first time,

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.863
I will this time, I
hope he's got a chance.

00:08:06.409 --> 00:08:08.140
I mean I've never known a president

00:08:08.140 --> 00:08:12.920
to go into office and
so many of his own party

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.993
be so much against him.

00:08:17.142 --> 00:08:21.193
And wouldn't let him do what
he said he was gonna do.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.880
Like I said, he talked a good talk,

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.330
that's what put him in there.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:31.420
But if he gets in there
again on the next go around,

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:33.110
I hope that he can go ahead

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:36.520
and do what he set out to do,

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.550
especially with the border wall.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.830
We've got a bad problem with immigration,

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.210
and dealing with China,
I think that was one

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.690
of the worst things we ever done

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.408
was passed that NAFTA bill

00:08:48.408 --> 00:08:50.520
that free trade agreement,
because it took a lot

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.140
of our textile workers,

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.510
our jobs away from the textile workers,

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.800
and sent them to China, Mexico,

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.030
and you can't even go to
a store and buy anything

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.870
that's not made in China, Taiwan, Mexico,

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:04.710
and especially clothes.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.630
I remember Rocky Boots and stuff,

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:11.320
I hunt a lot and I always tried

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.510
to have a good pair of insulated boots,

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:17.490
and even Rocky Boot company,
they're made in China now.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.970
I mean, they need to, we need a president

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.540
that will bring our jobs back

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.290
and I think the country
would be better off

00:09:26.414 --> 00:09:29.840
and give the people here the opportunity

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.973
to go back to work.

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:36.000
If they would stop the
immigrants from coming in here,

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.423
that would make a big difference.

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.230
Finish that border wall.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.653
I mean I'm all for that.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:46.270
- [Interviewer] Do you have children?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.825
- No sir.

00:09:47.825 --> 00:09:48.658
- [Interviewer] No kids, you're married?

00:09:48.658 --> 00:09:49.491
- No sir.
- No?

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.090
- [Interviewer] What are you
proudest of in your life?

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.370
- Sorry?
- What are you proudest of

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:55.560
in your life?
- What am I proud of?

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.230
Well I'm proud that I'm white,

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.470
that's one of the main things I'm proud of

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:03.240
and I'm proud that I come
from the family I came from

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.460
with the background

00:10:05.882 --> 00:10:07.950
and I've got ancestors that fought

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.436
in the Civil War for the South,

00:10:10.436 --> 00:10:14.860
I mean everybody says that
slavery was the main issue

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.740
in the Civil War.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.490
It could've been part, but myself,

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:23.700
I think it was mainly over
the money and state's rights.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:25.980
We had the cotton, the tobacco,

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.330
all the agriculture down here.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:31.240
And taxes, they probably
wasn't paying the taxes

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:35.183
on their stuff and but that's,

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:37.970
if I can make a dollar and get by with it,

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:38.813
I'm gonna do it.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
They knew that once they
pulled from the Union,

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.880
when the southern states seceded,

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:49.230
that's what they were seceding over.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:54.230
The taxes, states rights and
I'm not gonna leave slavery out

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.160
I'm sure slavery had a part to do with it,

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.650
but the North had slaves,
we got a lot of our slaves

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.170
from the North.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:07.170
Even our presidents, Grant,
when he became president,

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.740
he didn't give up his slaves
until he got nominated

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:14.290
to be president, I mean.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:16.130
Then he gave his slaves up, what?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.443
Four, five years after the civil war?

00:11:20.276 --> 00:11:23.610
I mean they just, they tell,

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.163
just like Robert E. Lee said,

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:30.820
the victors of war will write the story.

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.540
And I remember growing up in school,

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.270
all the books that we studied in school

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.120
was published from up North.

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.780
They wasn't none of the books
published from down here.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.360
They tell you what they want you to learn,

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:44.600
and that's why the people today,

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:49.274
they don't know their history,
if the blacks had any clue,

00:11:49.274 --> 00:11:50.930
and if they had had enough sense

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:54.250
to open a book and study history,

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:55.730
they wouldn't be going out here and voting

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:58.190
these democrat tickets, because the Klan

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:02.430
was founded by democrats,
a republican freed 'em.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:06.460
But they're so much against
the republican party,

00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:09.557
the part that freed 'em, you know?

00:12:09.557 --> 00:12:11.720
It's got a lot to do with the history

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:14.342
and they're not teaching it in the school

00:12:14.342 --> 00:12:16.040
and that's what our younger
generation's gonna grow up

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.062
to see, a bunch of lies.

00:12:19.062 --> 00:12:22.473
That's my opinion, I'll go
to my grave feeling that way,

00:12:23.957 --> 00:12:28.957
and it's a shame what
we're gonna leave the kids

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.690
for the future, the
shape it's gonna be in,

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.650
this country's, I see every day,

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.100
it's getting worse and worse.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.293
- [Interviewer] Were there
every lynchings in the Klan?

00:12:43.683 --> 00:12:45.533
- Well I'm sure there were years ago.

00:12:46.738 --> 00:12:49.980
There have not been no
lynches in, I'm gonna say,

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.650
50, 60 years.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.600
But most of the lynchings
was more down south.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:58.313
Like I said, a lot of the
other Klan groups years ago,

00:12:59.221 --> 00:13:00.430
they did give us a bad name.

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:03.540
But as far as lynching going on today, no.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.730
You couldn't get by with it.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.013
- [Interviewer] One of the things

00:13:07.013 --> 00:13:09.259
that's interesting about Klansmen,

00:13:09.259 --> 00:13:10.890
is that they're so committed
to what they believe.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:13.018
- Oh I'm into what I believe.

00:13:13.018 --> 00:13:16.360
I got a heart of a
Klansman, and I will die

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.310
for a Klansman fighting for my race.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.901
- [Interviewer] I mean
you may believe things

00:13:20.901 --> 00:13:21.734
that other people may have
a hard time swallowing,

00:13:21.734 --> 00:13:23.340
but you believe what you believe

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:24.173
and you stand behind it.

00:13:24.173 --> 00:13:25.683
- Exactly, yes sir.

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:30.900
I believe that God, he
gave his life for our sins,

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.800
I believe in God.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.760
And as long as I've got God on my side,

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.240
I'm all right, as long as I believe

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:39.820
that I've got God in my heart,

